# current-projects — one entry per line: owner/repo [placement]
#
# Placement is optional and names the filesystem root the repo lives on:
#   (omitted)   /mnt/c/Users/alexa/Projects  — the default; Cowork can see it
#   ext4        $HOME/Projects               — build-heavy repos (ADR-0001)
#   /abs/path   an explicit root
#
# ADR-0001 splits repos across two filesystems: anything with node_modules, a
# bundler, or a file watcher stays on ext4, because inotify does not fire for
# Windows-side writes and watch mode then breaks silently. Marking such a repo
# 'ext4' is what stops sync-projects cloning a second copy onto /mnt/c — the
# divergence that produced wodgenerator and FileParser.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# Managed by: scripts/new-project (auto-appends on create)
# To sync: scripts/sync-projects

